{{Description}}

{{ToonInfo|Toon=Poppy|extra=Bubble|Pronoun=She|Date=June 14th, 2024|type=Single}}

==Appearance==
Pоppy is a cyan bubble with lighter inner highlights. She has two eyelashes on the outside corners of each eye and a smaller bubble on the lower back of her head that resembles a bun. Her body is outlined in a slightly darker cyan. An oversized, pink bow with a yellow middle piece is on top of her head, and she wears a pink dress that consists of a simple sleeveless bodice and bell-shaped skirt. Additionally, she wears yellow thigh high socks with pink stripes.

==Personality==
Poppy is a bubbly and energetic [[Toon]], loud and often speaking with multiple exclamation marks or even in caps. She is self-confident, not easily fazed, and she describes herself not as happy, but "optimistic". Her appearance is kept with care and modesty, and she frequently compliments others, sometimes suggesting additions and changes. She is prone to ditziness, believing {{CI|Vee|name=true}} about an improbable prize, not hearing {{CI|Shelly|name=true}}, and forgetting {{CI|Brightney|name=true}}'s lampshade color. It is also confirmed that she is great friends with {{CI|Looey|name=true}}.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/969934252844138499/1314757242465026139</ref>

It is heavily implied that Poppy is addicted to {{II|Pop|name=true}}, a brand that she is seemingly used as a mascot or advertisement for. This can be seen in her room in the [[Roleplay Mode]], where there are multiple {{II|Bottle o' Pop|name=false|plural=a}} and Pops in the shelves behind her bed's headboard, and also in her dialogue with {{CI|Astro|name=true}}, where he is worried she is losing sleep due to her addiction, whereas she replies with no care for her health.

==Mastery==
{{Mastery|Finish 30 [[Machines]]|Activate This [[Toon]]'s Passive Ability 30 times|Pick Up 30 [[Items]]|Survive 25 [[Floors]]|Use 30 Items|Travel 50000 Meters}}

===Mastery Strategies===
{{MastComp|{{MastStrat|first|Machine}}|{{MastStrat|second|you can start multiple solo runs and get repeatedly hit by [[Twisteds]] until you die, and then repeat. Let healer [[Toons]] (maybe more than one) like {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}} (recommended), {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} or {{CI|Ginger|name=true}} join your run and heal you to be able to get hit again and speed up the time. This strategy helps both yours '''and''' the healer's [[Masteries]] (if uncompleted). Doing this task may also help with the '''sixth task''' if you walk around while being hit}}|{{MastStrat|third and fifth|Collect and use|Use}}|{{MastStrat|fourth|Reach/do floors}}|{{MastStrat|sixth|Meters|3Star}}}}

==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first and only requirement, since Poppy is one of the starter [[Toons]], you can just select her for free on the Start Toon Selection screen.
*If {{CI|Boxten|name=true}} was chosen instead, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increase the further you descend, so you can earn more {{TI|Ichor|name=true}}.

==Strategies==
Poppy is a great choice for beginning players. Her [[Stealth]] and [[Movement Speed]], along with her [[Ability]], '''Panic Pop''', provide good recovery from mistakes, making her ideal for learning the basics. As an all-rounder [[Toon]], she does not specialize as a Distractor or Extractor but leans towards being a Survivalist with her Ability to outrun [[Twisteds]]. For optimal performance, it is recommended to equip her with Extraction-based [[Trinkets]] such as {{TI|Wrench|name=true}} and speed-enhancing Trinkets like {{TI|Pink Bow|name=true}}. This combination effectively improves her Movement and [[Extraction Speed]], and is easily accessible early on in the game, making it ideal for new players. Other helpful Trinkets that new players will find easy to acquire include {{TI|Speedy Shoes|name=true}} and {{TI|Party Popper|name=true}}.

Her Ability really helps against specific Twisteds like {{CI|Twisted Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}}, {{CI|Twisted Rodger|name=true}}, or {{CI|Twisted Vee|name=true}}, since the huge speed boost can make escape far easier. Twisted Razzle & Dazzle's circle is quite large, so escaping it when they're enraged could be quite difficult without potentially taking multiple hits (whether from multiple Twisteds or the aforementioned twins themselves) for some other Toons, but Poppy can escape the circle with ease when injured. Twisted Rodger and Twisted Vee can slow Poppy to the point where she can't outrun certain threats, but her speed boost can counteract the {{Debuff|Slow}}, allowing her to avoid taking multiple hits. While these are advantages she has, other Toons can have a similar experience thanks to their Abilities or Stats, and certain Trinkets like {{TI|Train Whistle|name=true}} could also help make things easier without needing to take a hit in the first place.

This Toon is less advantageous for experienced players, since her Ability only activates upon losing a Heart, limiting its overall viability and contributions. It is most effective for experienced players when dealing with large swarms of Twisteds, especially if multiple healers are present. If you are confident in your kiting abilities and tend to adapt quickly to new games, consider selecting {{CI|Boxten|name=true}} as your starter instead. For those who enjoy playing as Poppy, transitioning to {{CI|Looey|name=true}} might be the next step to take to enhance your experience.

If a teammate cannot escape a Twisted—whether because they are playing as a slower Toon, being chased by a fast Twisted like {{CI|Twisted Pebble|name=true}}, or are low on [[Stamina]]—it may be a viable strategy to intervene by taking a hit from the chasing Twisteds. This is especially effective if {{TI|Blushy Bat|name=true}} and/or {{TI|Soul Sword|name=true}} is equipped. By doing this, the player can provide both themself and their teammate an opportunity to escape, even if significant Stamina has been expended to reach them. This strategy may not be as efficient as using an {{II|Air Horn|name=true}} or good positioning—since it sacrifices a Heart to ensure their escape—but it is worthwhile in situations where low-health {{Type|Main}} Toons like {{CI|Shelly|name=true}} or {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} are in clear danger. Their Abilities are invaluable to the team, with Sprout even being able to heal the player afterward, mitigating the cost of the sacrifice. Inexperienced players '''should not''' attempt this strategy, as there are many intricacies that may turn this into sabotage rather than a rescue. Instead, wait and learn; surviving is enough in the beginning.

If a player find themself in a situation where they cannot reach the [[Elevator]] in time during [[Panic Mode]], it is advisable to walk in order to conserve or regenerate Stamina before intentionally taking a hit. Afterward, they can sprint to the Elevator. Failing to reach the Elevator in time results in an instant death, whereas losing one or two Hearts to Twisteds provides an opportunity for survival.

Note Poppy isn't the best choice for runs attempting to spawn {{CI|Twisted Dyle|name=true}}. Her Ability becomes far less useful due to his insta-kill and {{Type|Common}} Twisteds being easier to avoid than others. Her Stats don't provide any specific strengths by base either, with mediocre extraction or average mobility.

Due to her all-rounded Stats, any [[Items]] can be useful for her. Mobility Items such as {{II|Pop|name=false|plural=a}} and {{II|Speed Candy|name=false|plural=a}} can make escape easier, keeping her Ability as a last resort. Extraction Items like {{II|Instructions|name=false}} and {{II|Skill Check Candy|name=false|plural=a}} can improve her average extraction, filling Machines more efficiently. Healing Items can help for newer players who get hit more often (unless there's a healer on the team), or to make a body blocking playstyle more safe (though this can eat through heals).

Overall, Poppy is a good starter Toon, but is heavily outclassed later in the game by Toons who have better extraction and escapability. She has a couple niches, but struggles to really shine when other Toons can more effectively fulfill them.

===Trinket Combinations===
{{Preference}}For specific [[Trinket]] recommendations, here are some possible combinations:

====Survivability====
*'''{{TI|Pink Bow|name=true}}/Options'''
**This Trinket enables Poppy to outrun all Twisteds outside of Panic Mode besides {{CI|Twisted Dyle|name=true}} at max speed {{Small|(26.9 run speed/40.3 when attacked)}}. Here are some options to pair Pink Bow with:
***'''{{TI|Speedy Shoes|name=true}}''', to further improve run speed {{Small|(28.2 run speed/42.34 when attacked)}};
***'''{{TI|Vanity Mirror|name=true}}''', to outrun every Twisted except Twisted Dyle during Panic Mode {{Small|(35 run speed/52.4 when attacked)}};
***'''{{TI|Train Whistle|name=true}}''', to make escaping with the {{Debuff|Slow|}}Debuff easier without losing much Stamina;
***Any of the Trinkets in the '''Extraction Section''', to help with [[Floor]] progression; etc.

====Extraction====
*'''{{TI|Magnifying Glass|name=true}}/Options'''
**This Trinket allows Poppy to take full advantage over her 3{{Star}} [[Extraction Speed]] {{Small|(1.00 extraction speed)}} and [[Skill Check]] {{Small|(100.5 skill check size)}}. Here are some options to pair Magnifying Glass with:
***'''{{TI|Vee's Remote|name=true}}''', to allow for quicker Floor progression, especially if teammates also carry Vee's Remote;
***'''{{TI|Participation Award|name=true}}''', to speed up [[Machine]] completion by maximizing Skill Check extraction {{Small|(25.57 avg/23.26 with Tech Savvy)}};
***Any Trinkets listed in the '''Survivability/Mobility''' section, to help with survival.

====Other====
*'''{{TI|Blushy Bat|name=true}}/Any'''
**Blushy Bat synergizes incredibly well with Poppy's Passive Ability. Due to its accessibility, this Trinket is a must-have for newer players, giving them a generous amount of time to get distance from Twisteds after a hit. Experienced players are more likely to benefit more from the other recommended Trinkets above.
*'''{{TI|Soul Sword|name=true}}/Any'''
**Soul Sword, like Blushy Bat, synergizes greatly with Poppy's Ability. Its speed boost will assist her in escaping Twisteds while Soul Sword slows them down, allowing for easy escapes. This Trinket could also be paired with Blushy Bat to almost guarantee safe escapes, though it does take both Trinket slots, and the Trinkets can counteract each other a bit.

