==Trivia==
*At the end of the [[Poppy/Gallery#Development|Meet Poppy Teaser Video]], morse code can be heard that translates to "KEEP YOUR ALLIES CLOSE."
**This is also one of the texts that can appear when starting a new run {{Small|(at the bottom of the elevator screen)}}.
**In the same video, {{CI|Dandy|name=true}} is seen with Poppy and the former's {{CI|Twisted Dandy}}[[Twisted Dandy|Twisted counterpart]]'s song can be heard throughout the video.
*Poppy appears to be a marketing mascot for a soft drink company, as she is printed on every vending machine in all of the [[Floors]]. The company is also trademarked as "'''Poppy Pop'''".
**This could be the reason she likes drinking {{II|Pop|name=true}}, something seen in her room in the [[Roleplay Mode]].
*Her name, Poppy, is a pun on both the feminine name Poppy and her status as a bubble, which not only pops easily when touched but also produces a popping sound.
*Poppy's favorite tea is {{wp|bubble tea}}, as shown in her interaction with {{CI|Teagan|name=true}}.
**This could reflect herself, as a bubble.
*Poppy is designation ''SC-003'', with the '''SC''' standing for Side Character.
**Before [[Changelog|v0.12]], she used to be ''C-001'', with C maybe meaning {{Type|Common}}, possibly hinting she may have been the first Common [[Toon]] made.
***Since the [[2025 Christmas Event]], {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}} was revealed as the actual first Common Toon made in {{CI|Bobette|name=true}}'s [[Gossip]] about him.
*Poppy doesn't know how to drive, as confirmed in her interaction with {{CI|Vee|name=true}}.
*Poppy is not good at cleaning, as confirmed in her interaction with {{CI|Tisha|name=true}}.
*A small doodle of her and {{CI|Toodles|name=true}} can be found pinned on her vanity mirror in her room over on [[Roleplay Mode]]. This could possibly hint at a close relationship between the two.
**{{CI|Boxten|name=true}}'s interaction with Toodles implies that Toodles was the one who drew it.
*Though Poppy and [[Boxten]] seem to be good friends, [[Qwel]] has said they have no confirmed relations.
**They share a lot of similarities.
***Most (if not all) of their similarities are due to them being the starters [[Toons]] of the game.
****Whoever isn't chosen as the player's first Toon costs 100 {{TI|Ichor|name=true}}, therefore, they both have no other requirements except for a certain amount of Ichor.
*****The Price use to be 250 Ichor each before being reduced at an unknown time.
***They both have 3{{Star}} on all of their [[Stats]] and share the same Stat spread with all of the {{Type|Common}} [[Event Toons]].
****{{CI|Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}} could also count if not considering their [[Abilities]], though only in the Toon selection.
***Both of their [[Twisted]] counterparts are {{Type|Common}}, have average Stats, and no special abilities to aid them.
***They both have an official [[merchandise]] plush.
***Both their respective [[Trinkets]], respectively {{TI|Pink Bow|name=true}} and {{TI|Blue Bandana|name=true}}, are present in their models and have mechanics that resemble their Abilities, even being able to directly stack with their Ability boosts.
***They have 4 [[Mastery]] quests in common, being "Pick 30 [[Items]]!", "Survive 25 [[Floors]]!", "Use 30 Items!", and "Travel 50000 Meters!".
****For their other quests, Boxten needs to finish 20 more [[Machines]] than Poppy does, and Poppy needs to activate her Ability 30 times, while Boxten needs to survive a Floor with all 8 players alive (which also reflects his Ability, since it's where he would get to his full potential).
***They both have [[Skins]] whose skin color doesn't change, being {{Skin|Sapphire Dots}} and {{Skin|Creepy Chord}} respectively.
***Both their [[Christmas]] Skins, respectively {{Skin|Confident Caroler}} and {{Skin|Quiet Caroler}}, are probably meant to match for being both "carolers".
***They both have 2 interactions with {{CI|Looey|name=true}}.
***They got optimized in the same [[update]], along with [[Cosmo]], {{CI|Sprout|name=true}}, and [[Dandy]].
***When bought in [[Dandy's Store]], Dandy says "_ is a great choice!" for both of them.
***They both have "Meet _" teaser videos with morse code at the end of each one.
*Poppy is one of the first Common [[Toons]] that weren't previously optimized to receive an optimized model, with the others being [[Boxten]] and [[Cosmo]].
**She is also the first female Toon to do so.
*Poppy and [[Looey]] are friends.<ref>https://discord.com/channels/969934252844138496/969934252844138499/1314757242465026139</ref>
**Poppy's [[Mastery]] being needed to unlock Looey, their Passive [[Abilities]] similarities (both gaining additional [[Movement Speed]] by taking damage), their material similarities (fragile spheres), and their respective [[Trinkets]]' mechanics similarities can also reflect this.
*Poppy is the first [[Toon]] to activate/use an [[Ability]] by taking damage, with the second being [[Cosmo]], the third being [[Looey]], and the fourth being {{CI|Yatta|name=true}}.
**{{CI|Pebble|name=true}} was also the first before his rework in [[Changelog|v0.3]].
***{{CI|Ginger|name=true}} was the fourth before her rework in the [[2025 Christmas Event]].
*In the starter [[Toon]] menu added in [[Changelog|v0.22.1]], Poppy's face is comprised of multiple 3D assets for her eyes and mouth instead of 2D textures. This was likely to make the facial expressions easier to do without tons of textures being needed.

